ily, was elected prince of Bulgaria in 1887.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-i-of-leon"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ferdinand-i-of-leon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ferdinand I of León</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ferdinand I, called the Great, was a son of Sancho III of Navarre who received the county of Castile and became king of León in 1037 after killing Bermudo III in battle.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-i-of-naples"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ferdinand-i-of-naples.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ferdinand I of Naples</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ferdinand I, known as Ferrante, was King of Naples from 1458 to 1494, the illegitimate son of Alfonso V of Aragon.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-i-of-romania"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ferdinand-i-of-romania.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ferdinand I of Romania</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ferdinand I of Romania, of the Hohenzollern-Sigmaringen family, succeeded his uncle Carol I in 1914.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-i-of-the-two-sicilies"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ferdinand-i-of-the-two-sicilies.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ferdinand I of the Two Sicilies</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ferdinand I of the Two Sicilies was a Bourbon king who ruled Naples as Ferdinand IV from 1759.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-i-holy-roman-emperor"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ferdinand-i-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ferdinand I, Holy Roman Emperor</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ferdinand I was the younger brother of Charles V, who gave him the Austrian lands in 1521.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-ii-of-aragon"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ferdinand-ii-of-aragon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ferdinand II of Aragon</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ferdinand II of Aragon was king of Aragon whose marriage to Isabella of Castile united the two crowns.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-ii-of-the-two-sicilies"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ferdinand-ii-of-the-two-sicilies.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ferdinand II of the Two Sicilies</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ferdinand II of the Two Sicilies was the Bourbon king of Naples and Sicily from 1830 to 1859.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-ii-archduke-of-austria"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ferdinand-ii-archduke-of-austria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ferdinand II, Archduke of Austria</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ferdinand II, Archduke of Austria, was a son of Emperor Ferdinand I who ruled Tyrol and Further Austria from 1564.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-ii-holy-roman-emperor"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ferdinand-ii-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ferdinand II, Holy Roman Emperor</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ferdinand II, Holy Roman Emperor, was the son of Archduke Charles II of Inner Austria and ruled from Graz before becoming emperor in 1619.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-iii-of-castile"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ferdinand-iii-of-castile.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ferdinand III of Castile</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ferdinand III was king of Castile and later León in the thirteenth century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-iii-grand-duke-of-tuscany"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ferdinand-iii-grand-duke-of-tuscany.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ferdinand III, Grand Duke of Tuscany</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ferdinand III, Grand Duke of Tuscany, was a Habsburg prince who lost Tuscany to the French in 1799.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-iii-holy-roman-emperor"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ferdinand-iii-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ferdinand III, Holy Roman Emperor</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ferdinand III, Holy Roman Emperor, of the Habsburg dynasty, reigned from 1637 to 1657.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-magellan"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ferdinand-magellan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ferdinand Magellan</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ferdinand Magellan was a Portuguese navigator who led a Spanish expedition from 1519 to find a western route to the Spice Islands.</span></a></li></ul>
